{"allowed_modes":["walk","fly","instantly"],"category":"Architectural style","citations":[{"archived_url":"","citation":"'1612 S. Prairie Ave.' Photograph of the Joseph Goodman (later Studebaker, then Bishop Anderson) house, 1612 South Prairie Avenue, Chicago, from the south-east on the Prairie Avenue walk; unknown photographer, undated. Reproduced on chicagology.com, Prairie Avenue, 1612 S. Prairie.","source_id":"chicagology_1612_prairie_photo","tier":1,"tier_label":"period/eyewitness","url":"https://chicagology.com/chicagostreets/prairieavenue/1612prairie/","what_it_does_not_supply":["colour: the print is monochrome, so the stone's kind and every paint colour stay reconstructed","the roof: nothing of it shows over the cornice from the walk","the side, rear and north walls beyond the front bay of the south wall","a date: undated, and its 1904 reading rests on nothing recorded as changing"],"what_it_supplies":["the bay count, the entrance's bay and the arrangement of every street-front window, by storey","the round heads, the radiating voussoir joints and the keystones","the principal floor's belt, the storey lines and the stone's top, as heights through the camera solve","the frieze with its lights, under a bracketed cornice","the frontispiece and the arched portico on columns","the iron guards, basement grilles and front fence"]},{"archived_url":"","citation":"'Lost Houses of Prairie Avenue: 1600-1700 Blocks', Prairie Avenue Historic District interpretive marker, Chicago; transcription on the Historical Marker Database (HMdb), marker 308722.","source_id":"hmdb_prairie_lost_houses_1600_1700","tier":4,"tier_label":"later scholarship","url":"https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=308722","what_it_does_not_supply":["the 1904 occupants","any measurement or appearance"],"what_it_supplies":["each house's builder, year built and architect as the district's marker gives them","Pullman's theatre, organ and bowling alley and Beman's conservatory additions, in paraphrase"]},{"archived_url":"","citation":"'Lost Houses of Prairie Avenue: 1800-1900 Blocks (West Side)', Prairie Avenue Historic District interpretive marker, Chicago; transcription on the Historical Marker Database (HMdb), marker 308706.","source_id":"hmdb_prairie_lost_houses_1800_1900_west","tier":4,"tier_label":"later scholarship","url":"https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=308706","what_it_does_not_supply":["measurements or appearance beyond the style named"],"what_it_supplies":["year built, architect and style as the marker states them for 1808, 1812, 1824, 1834, 1912 and 1936 Prairie"]}],"content_version":1,"default_mode":"walk","endings":[{"completion_eligible":true,"id":"finish","read_s":10,"text":"End of the Italianate walk. Brackets under the eaves and round-headed windows are the marks to look for on the older fronts of the avenue."}],"evidence":[{"confidence":"attested","id":"goodman-marker","locator":"The 1612 S. Prairie Avenue entry's name line.","sources":["hmdb_prairie_lost_houses_1600_1700"],"text":"Joseph Goodman Residence. Built 1869; architect unknown."},{"confidence":"attested","id":"goodman-photo","locator":"The whole print: the stone street front from its south corner to its north corner, the stoop and the portico.","sources":["chicagology_1612_prairie_photo"],"text":"The photograph shows a three-bay stone front, every window round-headed under voussoirs with a long keystone, a belt course at the principal floor, and an arched portico on columns at the head of a high stoop."},{"confidence":"inferred","id":"goodman-style","reasoning":"Round-headed windows under keystoned voussoirs, a belt course and an arched portico on a high stoop are the Italianate vocabulary of an 1869 stone front; the T-1837 register files the house Italianate stone-front masonry.","sources":["chicagology_1612_prairie_photo"],"text":"The front is read as Italianate."},{"confidence":"reconstructed","id":"hibbard-draft","liberty":"L-draft-prairie-16-18-east-2335","sources":[],"text":"The district draft reads the Hibbard house from the T-1837 register as an Italianate mansion with a rear addition: a low hip on bracketed eaves over a stone-based body, and the 1874 rear range."},{"confidence":"attested","id":"hibbard-marker","locator":"The 1701 S. Prairie Avenue entry: its name line, and its description as read in paraphrase.","sources":["hmdb_prairie_lost_houses_1600_1700"],"text":"William G. Hibbard Residence. Built 1869; William Le Baron Jenney, architect; Hibbard was president of a large wholesale hardware firm (read in paraphrase)."},{"confidence":"attested","id":"jones-marker","locator":"The 1834 S. Prairie Avenue entry.","sources":["hmdb_prairie_lost_houses_1800_1900_west"],"text":"Fernando Jones Residence. Built 1866; John M. Van Osdel, architect. In 1886, the Italianate residence received a mansard addition to bring it into fashion with many of its neighbors."},{"confidence":"reconstructed","id":"tolman-draft","liberty":"L-draft-prairie-20-22-east-2352","sources":[],"text":"The district draft reads 2031 Prairie as the north house of an 1869 Lemont-limestone row: an Italianate flat roof behind a bracketed cornice over three storeys; the row shares one cornice line, and its doors differ."},{"confidence":"reconstructed","id":"tour","liberty":"L-jaunt-prairie-walks","sources":[],"text":"The route, its order, its reading times, its keepsake and its framing are modern interpretation; no historical visit, conversation or occupant on 1 July 1904 is asserted."},{"confidence":"reconstructed","id":"walker-draft","liberty":"L-draft-prairie-16-18-west-2334","sources":[],"text":"The district draft reads the Tyrrell/Walker house from the T-1837 register as an Italianate frame house: a low hip on deep bracketed eaves, with a central gable, a canted bay and a full-width porch."}],"featured":false,"id":"prairie-style-italianate","keepsake":{"family":"News & Knowledge","id":"prairie-italianate-note","text":"A modern field note on the style's brackets and round heads, not a period document.","title":"Italianate field note"},"liberties":["L-draft-prairie-16-18-east-2335","L-draft-prairie-16-18-west-2334","L-draft-prairie-20-22-east-2352","L-jaunt-prairie-walks"],"opening":{"read_s":14,"text":"STYLE WALK: ITALIANATE. Look for tall round-headed windows, deep bracketed cornices and eaves, and high stoops. Five houses, 1612 to 2031 Prairie, on foot. Three are still first rough models, read from the district register."},"places":{"armour_corwith_house_1945_prairie":"Armour-Corwith House, 1945 Prairie","armour_corwith_house_1945_prairie_coach_house":"Armour-Corwith coach house, 1945 Prairie","armour_house_2115_prairie":"Kelley-Armour House, 2115 Prairie","armour_house_2115_prairie_coach_house":"Kelley-Armour coach house, 2115 Prairie","buckingham_house_2036_prairie":"Buckingham House, 2036 Prairie","buckingham_house_2036_prairie_coach_house":"Buckingham coach house, 2036 Prairie","coleman_ames_house_1811_prairie":"Coleman-Ames House, 1811 Prairie","coleman_ames_house_1811_prairie_coach_house":"Coleman-Ames coach house, 1811 Prairie","dent_house_1823_prairie":"Dent House, 1823 Prairie","dexter_house_1721_prairie":"Dexter House, 1721 Prairie","dexter_house_1721_prairie_coach_house":"Dexter coach house, 1721 Prairie","doane_house_1827_prairie":"Doane House, 1827 Prairie","doane_house_1827_prairie_coach_house":"Doane coach house, 1827 Prairie","edson_keith_house_1906_prairie":"Edson Keith House, 1906 Prairie","edson_keith_house_1906_prairie_coach_house":"Edson Keith coach house, 1906 Prairie","elbridge_keith_house_1900_prairie":"Elbridge Keith House, 1900 Prairie","elbridge_keith_house_1900_prairie_coach_house":"Elbridge Keith coach house, 1900 Prairie","flats_2127_prairie":"Flats, 2127 Prairie","forsyth_house_1635_prairie":"Forsyth House, 1635 Prairie","george_glessner_house_1706_prairie":"George Glessner House, 1706 Prairie","glessner_house":"Glessner House, 1800 Prairie","glessner_lee_house_1700_prairie":"Glessner-Lee House, 1700 Prairie","glessne