ows a three-bay stone front, every window round-headed under a long keystone, a belt course at the principal floor, and an arched portico on columns at the head of a high stoop."},{"destination":{"id":"hibbard_house_1701_prairie","kind":"structure"},"evidence":["hibbard-marker","hibbard-draft","tour"],"id":"hibbard","next":"walker","read_s":17,"text":"1701 Prairie. William G. Hibbard's house of 1869, by William Le Baron Jenney, read by the district register as an Italianate mansion: a low hipped roof on bracketed eaves over a stone-based body, with a rear range added in 1874."},{"destination":{"id":"walker_house_1720_prairie","kind":"structure"},"evidence":["walker-draft","tour"],"id":"walker","next":"jones","read_s":19,"text":"1720 Prairie. The Tyrrell and Walker house, read by the district register as an Italianate house built of wood: a low hip on deep bracketed eaves, a central gable, a canted bay and a full-width porch. Compare it with the brick and stone fronts around it."},{"destination":{"id":"jones_house_1834_prairie","kind":"structure"},"evidence":["jones-marker","tour"],"id":"jones","next":"tolman","read_s":17,"text":"1834 Prairie. Fernando Jones's house of 1866, by John M. Van Osdel, which the district marker calls Italianate. In 1886 it was given a mansard addition to keep up with its neighbours, so here the Italianate house wears a newer roof."},{"destination":{"id":"tolman_house_2031_prairie","kind":"structure"},"evidence":["tolman-draft","tour"],"id":"tolman","next":"finish","read_s":18,"text":"2031 Prairie. The north house of a row of three built in 1869 with Lemont limestone fronts, read by the district register as Italianate: a flat roof behind a bracketed cornice over three storeys. The row shares one cornice line, but its doors differ."}],"title":"Italianate style walk"}
